✅ What is instanceof in Java?
The instanceof keyword is used to check whether an object is an instance of a specific class or implements a specific interface — including marker interfaces (interfaces with no methods).

🧪 Syntax:
java
Copy
Edit
object instanceof ClassName
Returns:

true → if object is an instance of ClassName or a subclass.

false → otherwise.


✅ instanceof works for both:
1. Classes
You can use instanceof to check if an object is an instance of a specific class or its subclass.

java
Copy
Edit
class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {}

Animal a = new Dog();

System.out.println(a instanceof Dog);    // true
System.out.println(a instanceof Animal); // true
2. Interfaces
It also works to check if an object implements an interface, including marker interfaces.

java
Copy
Edit
interface Pet {}
class Cat implements Pet {}

Pet p = new Cat();

System.out.println(p instanceof Cat); // true
System.out.println(p instanceof Pet); // true

❗️Note:
instanceof returns false if the reference is null.

It checks actual object type, not the reference type.